755	881	743	743	I	0	" That I would not , upon any account , intentionally offend Madame Duval ; but that I have weighty , nay unanswerable reasons for detaining her grand - daughter at present in England ; the principal of which is , that it was the earnest desire of one to whose will she owes implicit duty . Madame Duval may be assured , that she meets with the utmost attention and tenderness ; that her education , however short of my wishes , almost exceeds my abilities ; and I flatter myself , when the time arrives that she shall pay her duty to her grand - mother , Madame Duval will find no reason to be dissatisfied with what has been done for her . "
1221	1261	1214	1214	he	61	" My friend , forget your resentment , in favour of your humanity;-a father , trembling for the welfare of his child , bequeaths her to your care . O Villars ! hear ! pity ! And relieve me ! "
